  "description": "Be realistic about task difficulty: - Set milestones: Break hard tasks into smaller, achievable steps. - Reassess easy tasks: Don’t rush through just because they seem simple. - Check your assumptions: Look at past experiences for patterns of over- or underestimation. Example: Planning a complex project? Start with a detailed breakdown to avoid feeling overwhelmed or underprepared.",
